WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.080
In democracies, leaders need the votes of
millions of people. Pleasing so many

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.690
people is incredibly difficult,
so democracies offer voters public

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:17.130
policy options in exchange for votes. But
in dictatorships, leaders only need the

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.820
loyalty of a select few,
so they purchase it with cash, sports

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.630
cars, or luxury real estate. All
dictatorships are — to some degree —

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:29.670
corruption-fuelled kleptocracies. This is
bad news for democracy, the rule of law,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:34.649
and free markets. To protect their stolen
wealth, kleptocrats abuse anonymous

00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:39.329
financial tools in Western democracies,
and hire Westerners to help them do it.

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:43.469
So how can we dismantle the ways in
which corrupt dictatorships abuse the

00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:48.030
virtues of democracy and capitalism? We
can attack kleptocracy by leveraging our

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:52.320
comparative advantages in transparency
and the rule of law. A key first step

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.309
would be to do away with the anonymous
shell company, a commonly used tool for

00:00:56.309 --> 00:01:00.660
facilitating international corruption. To
fight kleptocracy, we must consolidate

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.650
liberty where it already exists, and lead
the way to greater freedom and

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.940
prosperity around the world.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.210
What do you
think America should do to deal with

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:14.310
authoritarian corruption? Let us know in
our poll. Also, let us know what other

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:18.540
topics you'd like our scholars to cover
in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.479
subscribe for more research and videos
from AEI.

